aic8800: lower the BSP default debug log level to errors only

The radxa driver's BSP ships aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|
LOGTRACE, logging every level during firmware download and chip bring-up -- enough
to flood the console and obstruct a first-boot login. Unlike the fdrv's
aicwf_dbg_level, the BSP level is not a module_param, so it cannot be lowered at
load and must be changed here; lower it to LOGERROR (errors only). The fdrv level
is set from modprobe.d instead (etc/modprobe.d/aic8800.conf), since it is a
module_param.

This is the SDIO/BSP hunk of radxa's own fix-Lower-the-debugging-log-level.patch
(Feng Zhang <feng@radxa.com>). The full upstream patch also touches the PCIE/USB
trees this board does not build, and its USB hunk does not apply against our
curated SDIO patch subset, so it is carried here scoped to the SDIO BSP.

diff --git a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
--- a/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
+++ b/src/SDIO/driver_fw/driver/aic8800/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_main.c
@@ -15,7 +15,7 @@
 #define DRV_AUTHOR            "AICSemi"
 #define DRV_VERS_MOD          "1.0"

-int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR|LOGINFO|LOGDEBUG|LOGTRACE;
+int aicwf_dbg_level_bsp = LOGERROR;

 struct semaphore aicbsp_probe_semaphore;

